    "y": 408.99
   },
   "value": "Sarah – Ronnie and dad don’t get on well and there’s lots of shouting from both. Ronnie is better when dad is at work \nGemma – Ronnie’s school attendance is now 89% and school are worried as his attendance has always been good. Class teacher has noticed small changes in his mood and engagement in learning.  Ronnie has asked his teacher a few times to call mum as he has said mum was crying this morning. School have supported Ronnie at this time and no call has been made.\nSarah and nursery are concerned about Sams speech being delayed and is also not potty trained yet\nSarah shared she is feeling low and struggles to wake in the mornings which impact on getting the children ready and into school/nursery. \nIt was mentioned that she doesn’t like using phones as her anxiety is high at present .\nGemma – tried to explore in more depth, unfortunately Sarah became upset and we spoke about getting everyone together so she has support from family and agreed to have a meeting with other family members. \n\n                                                                    Sarah "
  },
